nodes.body:
@yewentao256 could you take another look? This supersedes #49827: I have reviewed the current diff, rebased it onto main and trimmed the scheduler restrictions/non-BIC changes. Fresh H100/TP1 checks pass for mixed prefill/decode, arbitrary partitions and public Qwen serving with cache off/on (200 requests, 6,400 complete logit hashes). The description includes the measured performance cost and validation limits; Blackwell and MRV2 remain unvalidated.

[Intel CI #14141](https://buildkite.com/vllm/intel-ci/builds/14141) has a KV-planning optimized-Python subprocess timeout and a quantization case whose ModelOpt NVFP4 source is unsupported on XPU. Those tests and the supported-format declaration are unchanged by this diff. Could someone with Intel CI access compare the two failing cases on base `8a8e2baa02cd` versus head `8c9ff7e60a7f`, using matched worker/dependency settings? I have a child-stack diagnostic for the timeout and would prefer to establish baseline behavior rather than bundle unrelated CI fixes here. Local pre-commit passes; the upstream pre-run check is eligibility-gated.

The normalization overlap with #57280 is disclosed in Related Work; happy to coordinate that during review. GEMM #60034 and TP #50299 remain separate follow-ups.

